==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Metal Macho''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
At first, Metal Cat doesn't seem to be worth using, but once the right level is reached, this cat becomes exceptional if used properly. Metal Cat can take a maximum of 12 hits when it is level 19 (which is the same at level 20) while having only 2 knockbacks, meaning that he can stop the progress of a single enemy, regardless of its attack power, by standing in front of it for 6 attacks twice. Hence, he is very useful against enemies with high power but slow attacks, like [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]], [[Filibuster Obstructa]] and [[THE SLOTH]], or can also deny a huge amount of hits from enemies like [[Teacher Cybear]].

However, what makes Metal Cat a good unit is also his downfall; as said before, Metal Cat will die after 12 hits, no matter how much damage each hit does, and when he falls, his long cooldown means you'll wait for quite a while before the next comes. When there are a lot of peons, instead of wasting 600¢, use your usual tough meatshields such as [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]] and [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Wall Cat]], or to make this problem minimal, clear the way with attackers like [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Macho Legs]]. Metal Cat should also not be used on stages featuring enemies with frequently hitting attacks such as [[Bore]], or enemies with [[Critical Hit]]s or [[Toxic]] attacks, like [[R.Ost]] or [[Zollow]] respectively.

Metal Cat has a higher than average XP exchange value, but is unable to convert dupes to + levels. While the XP is still a very large amount, it is recommended to keep him if you don't own the unit already, or save the dupes until after completing [[Into the Future]] to exchange for 15 NP, as NP can be much harder to accumulate than XP.

