==Trivia==
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Metal Macho was a part of two other [[Cat Combo]]s: [[Biceps (Removed Combo)|Biceps]] and [[Precious Metals (Removed Combo)|Precious Metals]].
*Prior to [[Version 14.1 Update|Version 14.1]], [[Neneko (Super Rare Cat)|Neneko]], [[Gold Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Gold Cat]], [[Cat Base Mini (Super Rare Cat)|Cat Base Mini]] and Metal Cat could only be unlocked when "Limited Edition" was part of the current pool.
*Metal Cat is the only Non-[[:Category:Normal Cats|Normal]] Cat that cannot be upgraded beyond level 20.
**Additionally, Metal Cat is the only [[:Category:Gacha Cats|gacha unit]] who cannot benefit from plus-levels. This means that his absolutely highest level is 20, which is the lowest maximum level in the game, aside from [[Cheetah Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Cheetah Cat]], who can only be obtained by cheating.
*Metal and [[Gold Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Gold Cat]] on their icons are slightly lower than Cat and [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Cat]].
**This is most noticeable on the removed combo [[Biceps (Removed Combo)|Biceps]].
*Even though he's a [[:Category:Super Rare Cats|Super Rare Cat]], Metal Cat's upgrading costs are those of an [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cat]].
*Metal Cat, [[Ototo Corps|Iron Wall Cat]] and [[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Glass Cat]] are currently the only cat units with the Metal ability.
*This and [[Gold Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Gold Cat]] are the only Super Rare Cats that can be exchanged for more than 478,000 XP. Metal Cat can be exchanged for 777,777 XP specifically.
*His Evolved Form's description doesn't show his weakness to Critical Attacks in both English and Japanese, even though his Normal Form does.

